# The in-tree always-loaded injection set, AS OBSERVED — not as modelled.
#
# Provenance: recorded 2026-08-06/07 from the injected `# claudeMd` context
# headers of three live agents, read out of their own contexts:
#   * weave  — cwd /home/coder/sprawl (the main checkout, no worktree)
#   * forge  — cwd /home/coder/sprawl/.sprawl/worktrees/forge (manager)
#   * hex    — cwd /home/coder/sprawl/.sprawl/worktrees/hex   (this agent)
#
# What the three headers agree on, and what makes this file necessary:
#
#   file             | root copy | worktree copy
#   -----------------|-----------|--------------
#   CLAUDE.md        | ABSENT    | present
#   CLAUDE.local.md  | present   | present
#
# Same directory, same ancestry, two files, opposite treatment. weave's header
# (at the root, with no worktree) DOES list the root CLAUDE.md, which kills the
# reading that it is skipped for some intrinsic reason: the rule is
# `CLAUDE.md` resolves to the NEAREST ancestor only, `CLAUDE.local.md`
# accumulates across ancestors. Both copies of CLAUDE.local.md load and are
# byte-identical, so the loader is not content-deduplicating either.
#
# `DESCRIPTION.md` and `AGENTS.md` are absent from all three headers. That is
# evidence, not silence: a manifest reports in both directions, so CLAUDE.md's
# prose "Read `DESCRIPTION.md`" demonstrably does not cause a load.
#
# This file is an oracle for the MODEL, not a live probe of the harness. It is
# what fires when the injected set changes shape — a claim about a harness
# version we do not control, which is why the tripwire is worth more than the
# model. If it fires: confirm against a live agent's context header FIRST, then
# re-record here.
#
# Out-of-tree entries are deliberately omitted: they are reported by the script
# but are not part of the enforced in-tree set.
# TRACKED-ONLY, since QUM-1155. This file records the ENFORCED set, which is the
# subset of the observed injections that are git-tracked in the sprawl root's
# index. Both CLAUDE.local.md copies were recorded here and are now deliberately
# ABSENT. Nothing above changed: they still load, the three headers still say so,
# and the resolver still reports them with their sizes under "in-tree but
# UNTRACKED".
#
# They are gone from THIS FILE because CLAUDE.local.md is gitignored and
# per-user. In a fresh clone it does not exist, so the resolver derives a set
# without it — and every recorded-but-not-derived entry is a FAILURE by design
# ("absence is trivially true"). The old recording therefore made a correct clean
# clone exit 1, measured on a --depth 1 clone of main. Do NOT re-add them, and do
# NOT add an [untracked] section: either one re-creates that failure, on every
# machine except the one that happens to hold the file.
#
# Consequence to accept rather than fix: the CLAUDE.local.md doubling is no
# longer pinned by this tripwire, because the doubled file is the untracked one.
# It is still pinned by the resolver's untracked report (which prints both copies
# with distinct paths) and by the multiplicity assertions in
# scripts/test-always-loaded-budget.sh.
#
# TWO perspectives, both observed, selected by where --root points. Recording
# only one makes the other false-fail, and "re-record" would then break the
# first — a ping-pong between two correct readings.

# An agent in a worktree (forge, hex, byte): of the three files that load, only
# the worktree CLAUDE.md is tracked. The two CLAUDE.local.md copies are reported,
# not enforced.
[worktree]
<worktree>/CLAUDE.md

# weave, at the main checkout with no worktree. This is still the observation
# that proves root CLAUDE.md is not skipped for an intrinsic reason — it loads
# here, and is shadowed by the nearer copy in a worktree.
[root]
CLAUDE.md
